  },
  {
   "id": "b27",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And more importantly, how they arise.",
   "directed": "And more importantly, how they arise."
  },
  {
   "id": "b28",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, if you’re expecting a straightforward explanation of how one thing produces another, I’ve got bad news.",
   "directed": "Now, if you’re expecting a straightforward explanation of how one thing produces another, I’ve got bad news."
  },
  {
   "id": "b29",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Abhinavagupta is about to challenge your entire understanding of cause and effect.",
   "directed": "Abhinavagupta is about to challenge your entire understanding of cause and effect."
  },
  {
   "id": "b30",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And then, once he’s finished dismantling causation, he’s going to explain exactly how Śiva becomes an individual with limited knowledge, attachment, a body, five senses and a rather unfortunate habit of thinking he’s separate from everything.",
   "directed": "And then, once he’s finished dismantling causation, he’s going to explain exactly how Śiva becomes an individual with limited knowledge, attachment, a body, five senses and a rather unfortunate habit of thinking he’s separate from everything."
  },
  {
   "id": "b31",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Let’s begin.",
   "directed": "Let’s begin."
  },
  {
   "id": "b32",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "1. What actually makes something a tattva?\nRight.",
   "directed": "1. What actually makes something a tattva?\nRight."
  },
