  {
   "id": "b935",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Viṣaya.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Viṣaya."
  },
  {
   "id": "b936",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So buddhi is a kind of meeting place.",
   "directed": "So buddhi is a kind of meeting place."
  },
  {
   "id": "b937",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The appearance of the subject and the appearance of the object are both presented within the intellectual principle.",
   "directed": "The appearance of the subject and the appearance of the object are both presented within the intellectual principle."
  },
  {
   "id": "b938",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now imagine looking at a flower.",
   "directed": "Now imagine looking at a flower."
  },
  {
   "id": "b939",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "There’s an apparent knower.",
   "directed": "There’s an apparent knower."
  },
  {
   "id": "b940",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And there’s a flower.",
   "directed": "And there’s a flower."
  },
  {
   "id": "b941",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And within buddhi, the flower becomes an object of cognition.",
   "directed": "And within buddhi, the flower becomes an object of cognition."
  },
  {
   "id": "b942",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But then something rather unfortunate occurs.",
   "directed": "But then something rather unfortunate occurs."
  },
  {
   "id": "b943",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because the next principle introduces a mistaken identification.",
   "directed": "Because the next principle introduces a mistaken identification."
  },
  {
   "id": "b944",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And this is one of the most important parts of the entire chapter.",
   "directed": "And this is one of the most important parts of the entire chapter."
  },
  {
   "id": "b945",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Ahaṃkāra.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Ahaṃkāra."
  },
  {
   "id": "b946",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The I-maker.",
   "directed": "The I-maker."
  },
  {
   "id": "b947",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "21. Ahaṃkāra — how the real “I” becomes the fake “I”\nRight.",
   "directed": "21. Ahaṃkāra — how the real “I” becomes the fake “I”\nRight."
  },
  {
   "id": "b948",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Let’s break down the word.",
   "directed": "Let’s break down the word."
  },
  {
   "id": "b949",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Aham.",
   "directed": "Aham."
  },
  {
   "id": "b950",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "I.",
   "directed": "I."
  },
  {
   "id": "b951",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Kāra.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Kāra."
  },
  {
   "id": "b952",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Maker, making.",
   "directed": "Maker, making."
  },
  {
   "id": "b953",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So:",
   "directed": "[short pause] So:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b954",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "I-maker.",
   "directed": "I-maker."
  },
  {
   "id": "b955",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now here’s the problem.",
   "directed": "Now here’s the problem."
  },
  {
   "id": "b956",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The pure consciousness of Śiva possesses genuine self-awareness.",
   "directed": "The pure consciousness of Śiva possesses genuine self-awareness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b957",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Aham-vimarśa.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Aham-vimarśa."
  },
  {
   "id": "b958",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The immediate apprehension of I.",
   "directed": "The immediate apprehension of I."
  },
  {
   "id": "b959",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not a conceptual identity.",
   "directed": "Not a conceptual identity."
  },
  {
   "id": "b960",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not a biography.",
   "directed": "Not a biography."
  },
  {
   "id": "b961",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not a name.",
   "directed": "Not a name."
  },
  {
   "id": "b962",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not an ego constructed through experience.",
   "directed": "Not an ego constructed through experience."
  },
  {
   "id": "b963",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The intrinsic self-awareness of consciousness.",
   "directed": "The intrinsic self-awareness of consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b964",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta says that this pure I-consciousness is:",
   "directed": "[short pause] And Abhinavagupta says that this pure I-consciousness is:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b965",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Apratiyogi.",
   "directed": "Apratiyogi."
  },
  {
   "id": "b966",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Without an opposing counterpart.",
   "directed": "Without an opposing counterpart."
  },
  {
   "id": "b967",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It isn’t the limited ego standing against a world of separate objects.",
   "directed": "It isn’t the limited ego standing against a world of separate objects."
  },
  {
   "id": "b968",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It’s the self-apprehension of unrestricted consciousness.",
   "directed": "It’s the self-apprehension of unrestricted consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b969",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Svātma-camatkāra.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Svātma-camatkāra."
  },
  {
   "id": "b970",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The wonder or delight of one’s own Self.",
   "directed": "The wonder or delight of one’s own Self."
  },
  {
   "id": "b971",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, what happens in ahaṃkāra?",
   "directed": "Now, what happens in ahaṃkāra?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b972",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The light of the subject comes into contact with the object reflected in buddhi.",
   "directed": "The light of the subject comes into contact with the object reflected in buddhi."
  },
  {
   "id": "b973",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And the limited individual mistakenly identifies something that is not the Self as the Self.",
   "directed": "And the limited individual mistakenly identifies something that is not the Self as the Self."
  },
  {
   "id": "b974",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Anātmani ātmābhimānaḥ.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Anātmani ātmābhimānaḥ."
  },
  {
   "id": "b975",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The attribution of Self to what is not Self.",
   "directed": "The attribution of Self to what is not Self."
  },
  {
   "id": "b976",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta gives a beautiful classical example.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta gives a beautiful classical example."
  },
  {
   "id": "b977",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "A piece of mother-of-pearl.",
   "directed": "A piece of mother-of-pearl."
  },
  {
   "id": "b978",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Śukti.",
   "directed": "Śukti."
  },
  {
   "id": "b979",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "You see it glistening.",
   "directed": "You see it glistening."
  },
  {
   "id": "b980",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And mistake it for silver.",
   "directed": "And mistake it for silver."
  },
  {
   "id": "b981",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The famous silver illusion.",
   "directed": "The famous silver illusion."
  },
  {
   "id": "b982",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, notice what’s happened.",
   "directed": "Now, notice what’s happened."
  },
  {
   "id": "b983",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Something genuinely appears.",
   "directed": "Something genuinely appears."
  },
  {
   "id": "b984",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "There’s a shining object.",
   "directed": "There’s a shining object."
  },
  {
   "id": "b985",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But you misidentify it.",
   "directed": "But you misidentify it."
  },
  {
   "id": "b986",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "You say:",
   "directed": "[short pause] You say:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b987",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“Silver!”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “Silver!”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b988",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "When in fact it’s mother-of-pearl.",
   "directed": "When in fact it’s mother-of-pearl."
  },
  {
   "id": "b989",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And similarly, the luminous reality of consciousness appears in association with the body, mind and differentiated faculties.",
   "directed": "And similarly, the luminous reality of consciousness appears in association with the body, mind and differentiated faculties."
  },
  {
   "id": "b990",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But the individual appropriates these limited appearances as the entirety of the Self.",
   "directed": "But the individual appropriates these limited appearances as the entirety of the Self."
  },
  {
   "id": "b991",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I am this body.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I am this body.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b992",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I am this intellect.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I am this intellect.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b993",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I am this particular personality.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I am this particular personality.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b994",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, Abhinavagupta makes a rather pointed criticism of Sāṃkhya.",
   "directed": "Now, Abhinavagupta makes a rather pointed criticism of Sāṃkhya."
  },
  {
   "id": "b995",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "He says Sāṃkhya doesn’t accept the true Self as possessing the same intrinsic I-awareness that his own tradition attributes to consciousness.",
   "directed": "He says Sāṃkhya doesn’t accept the true Self as possessing the same intrinsic I-awareness that his own tradition attributes to consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b996",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And that’s an important difference.",
   "directed": "And that’s an important difference."
  },
  {
   "id": "b997",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because for Trika, the pure I is not the problem.",
   "directed": "Because for Trika, the pure I is not the problem."
  },
  {
   "id": "b998",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The problem is the contraction of I-consciousness into a limited identity.",
   "directed": "The problem is the contraction of I-consciousness into a limited identity."
  },
  {
   "id": "b999",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The false identification.",
   "directed": "The false identification."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1000",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not self-awareness itself.",
   "directed": "Not self-awareness itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1001",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "This is absolutely fundamental.",
   "directed": "This is absolutely fundamental."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1002",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "You’re not trying to destroy the intrinsic aham of consciousness.",
   "directed": "You’re not trying to destroy the intrinsic aham of consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1003",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "You’re recognising that the limited ahaṃkāra is a constructed manifestation of a much deeper self-awareness.",
   "directed": "You’re recognising that the limited ahaṃkāra is a constructed manifestation of a much deeper self-awareness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1004",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta says the very word kāra in ahaṃkāra indicates its constructed character.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta says the very word kāra in ahaṃkāra indicates its constructed character."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1005",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It’s been made.",
   "directed": "It’s been made."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1006",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Formed.",
   "directed": "Formed."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1007",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Manifested.",
   "directed": "Manifested."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1008",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not the unrestricted I-consciousness itself.",
   "directed": "Not the unrestricted I-consciousness itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1009",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, this is probably the most important philosophical distinction in the chapter.",
   "directed": "Now, this is probably the most important philosophical distinction in the chapter."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1010",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because it’s the difference between:",
   "directed": "[short pause] Because it’s the difference between:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1011",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I am this limited organism.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I am this limited organism.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1012",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And:",
   "directed": "[short pause] And:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1013",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I am the consciousness in which this organism and its world appear.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I am the consciousness in which this organism and its world appear.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1014",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But Abhinavagupta doesn’t stop with the ego.",
   "directed": "But Abhinavagupta doesn’t stop with the ego."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1015",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because ahaṃkāra has further functions.",
   "directed": "Because ahaṃkāra has further functions."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1016",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And apparently we’re going to need quite a lot of them to build a functioning human being.",
   "directed": "And apparently we’re going to need quite a lot of them to build a functioning human being."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1017",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "22. From ahaṃkāra come your mind and senses\nNow Abhinavagupta distinguishes different aspects of ahaṃkāra.",
   "directed": "22. From ahaṃkāra come your mind and senses\nNow Abhinavagupta distinguishes different aspects of ahaṃkāra."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1018",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "There’s its role as an instrument.",
   "directed": "There’s its role as an instrument."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1019",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Karaṇa-skandha.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Karaṇa-skandha."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1020",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And its natural or constitutive side.",
   "directed": "And its natural or constitutive side."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1021",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Prakṛti-skandha.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Prakṛti-skandha."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1022",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The latter is differentiated according to the three guṇas.",
   "directed": "The latter is differentiated according to the three guṇas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1023",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sattva.",
   "directed": "Sattva."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1024",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Rajas.",
   "directed": "Rajas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1025",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Tamas.",
   "directed": "Tamas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1026",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Let’s begin with the predominantly sattvic aspect.",
   "directed": "Let’s begin with the predominantly sattvic aspect."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1027",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "From this arise:",
   "directed": "[short pause] From this arise:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1028",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Manas.",
   "directed": "Manas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1029",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The mind.",
   "directed": "The mind."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1030",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And the five powers of cognition.",
   "directed": "And the five powers of cognition."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1031",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Buddhīndriyas.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Buddhīndriyas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1032",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, manas is associated with the capacity relating to all the subtle sensory objects.",
   "directed": "Now, manas is associated with the capacity relating to all the subtle sensory objects."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1033",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But the individual senses have more particular capacities.",
   "directed": "But the individual senses have more particular capacities."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1034",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Hearing is connected with sound.",
   "directed": "Hearing is connected with sound."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1035",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sight with visible form.",
   "directed": "Sight with visible form."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1036",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Smell with odour.",
   "directed": "Smell with odour."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1037",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And so on.",
   "directed": "And so on."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1038",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now here’s a subtle but crucial point.",
   "directed": "Now here’s a subtle but crucial point."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1039",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The sense faculty is not simply identical with its physical organ.",
   "directed": "The sense faculty is not simply identical with its physical organ."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1040",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It’s the capacity through which a particular form of cognition occurs.",
   "directed": "It’s the capacity through which a particular form of cognition occurs."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1041",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta explicitly rejects an exclusively material account here.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta explicitly rejects an exclusively material account here."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1042",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because the cognitive faculty is connected with the I-maker.",
   "directed": "Because the cognitive faculty is connected with the I-maker."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1043",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Think of the sentence:",
   "directed": "[short pause] Think of the sentence:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1044",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Ahaṃ śṛṇomi.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Ahaṃ śṛṇomi."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1045",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "I hear.",
   "directed": "I hear."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1046",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not:",
   "directed": "[short pause] Not:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1047",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“My ear has independently manufactured some auditory data, and I’m receiving a report from it.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “My ear has independently manufactured some auditory data, and I’m receiving a report from it.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1048",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "No.",
   "directed": "No."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1049",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "“I hear.”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “I hear.”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1050",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The cognitive act is appropriated through ahaṃkāra.",
   "directed": "The cognitive act is appropriated through ahaṃkāra."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1051",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And because these faculties are instruments, karaṇas, they must be connected to the agent.",
   "directed": "And because these faculties are instruments, karaṇas, they must be connected to the agent."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1052",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Otherwise you’d need another instrument to connect the first instrument to the subject.",
   "directed": "Otherwise you’d need another instrument to connect the first instrument to the subject."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1053",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And another to connect that one.",
   "directed": "And another to connect that one."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1054",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And another.",
   "directed": "And another."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1055",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Congratulations.",
   "directed": "Congratulations."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1056",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Infinite regress again.",
   "directed": "Infinite regress again."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1057",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We dealt with this nonsense in Chapter One.",
   "directed": "We dealt with this nonsense in Chapter One."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1058",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Abhinavagupta isn’t having it.",
   "directed": "Abhinavagupta isn’t having it."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1059",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So the faculties of cognition operate as instruments associated with limited subjectivity.",
   "directed": "So the faculties of cognition operate as instruments associated with limited subjectivity."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1060",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But he also makes a further distinction.",
   "directed": "But he also makes a further distinction."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1061",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The principal powers of the limited individual are still:",
   "directed": "[short pause] The principal powers of the limited individual are still:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1062",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Vidyā, in relation to knowledge.",
   "directed": "Vidyā, in relation to knowledge."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1063",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And kalā, in relation to action.",
   "directed": "And kalā, in relation to action."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1064",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And their persistence can be appreciated even in someone who lacks ordinary vision or bodily movement.",
   "directed": "And their persistence can be appreciated even in someone who lacks ordinary vision or bodily movement."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1065",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The underlying subject and its fundamental capacities aren’t simply reducible to particular working physical organs.",
   "directed": "The underlying subject and its fundamental capacities aren’t simply reducible to particular working physical organs."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1066",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, here come the five cognitive faculties.",
   "directed": "Now, here come the five cognitive faculties."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1067",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Śrotra",
   "directed": "Śrotra"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1068",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Hearing",
   "directed": "Hearing"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1069",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Śabda — sound",
   "directed": "Śabda — sound"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1070",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Tvak",
   "directed": "Tvak"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1071",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Touch",
   "directed": "Touch"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1072",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sparśa — contact",
   "directed": "Sparśa — contact"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1073",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Cakṣus",
   "directed": "[slowly] Cakṣus"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1074",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sight",
   "directed": "Sight"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1075",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Rūpa — visible form",
   "directed": "Rūpa — visible form"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1076",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Jihvā",
   "directed": "[slowly] Jihvā"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1077",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Taste",
   "directed": "Taste"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1078",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Rasa — flavour",
   "directed": "Rasa — flavour"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1079",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Ghrāṇa",
   "directed": "[slowly] Ghrāṇa"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1080",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Smell",
   "directed": "Smell"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1081",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Gandha — odour",
   "directed": "Gandha — odour"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1082",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Lovely.",
   "directed": "[short pause] Lovely."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1083",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We’ve got a mind.",
   "directed": "We’ve got a mind."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1084",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And five ways of receiving experience.",
   "directed": "And five ways of receiving experience."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1085",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But now we need five ways of acting.",
   "directed": "But now we need five ways of acting."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1086",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta has an unusually interesting account of why there are precisely five.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta has an unusually interesting account of why there are precisely five."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1087",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "23. The five powers of action — why you can move, grab things and talk nonsense\nRight.",
   "directed": "23. The five powers of action — why you can move, grab things and talk nonsense\nRight."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1088",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The five action faculties are:",
   "directed": "[short pause] The five action faculties are:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1089",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Karmendriyas.",
   "directed": "Karmendriyas."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1090",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But here’s something interesting.",
   "directed": "But here’s something interesting."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1091",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "In this account, they also arise from the sattvic aspect of ahaṃkāra, particularly where certain subtle-object capacities predominate.",
   "directed": "In this account, they also arise from the sattvic aspect of ahaṃkāra, particularly where certain subtle-object capacities predominate."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1092",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, that’s not identical with every other Indian philosophical explanation.",
   "directed": "Now, that’s not identical with every other Indian philosophical explanation."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1093",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta explicitly acknowledges variant classifications shortly afterward.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta explicitly acknowledges variant classifications shortly afterward."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1094",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But first, let’s understand his own argument.",
   "directed": "But first, let’s understand his own argument."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1095",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Take the act of walking.",
   "directed": "Take the act of walking."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1096",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "You say:",
   "directed": "[short pause] You say:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1097",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Ahaṃ gacchāmi.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Ahaṃ gacchāmi."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1098",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "I go.",
   "directed": "I go."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1099",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, the faculty of movement is associated with:",
   "directed": "[short pause] Now, the faculty of movement is associated with:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1100",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Pāda-indriya.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Pāda-indriya."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1101",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The power whose principal physical location is the feet.",
   "directed": "The power whose principal physical location is the feet."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1102",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But that doesn’t mean the metaphysical faculty is absolutely restricted to the physical feet.",
   "directed": "But that doesn’t mean the metaphysical faculty is absolutely restricted to the physical feet."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1103",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "A person who cannot walk may still possess capacities for movement.",
   "directed": "A person who cannot walk may still possess capacities for movement."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1104",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And the power of movement isn’t necessarily annihilated because a particular bodily organ is damaged.",
   "directed": "And the power of movement isn’t necessarily annihilated because a particular bodily organ is damaged."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1105",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, Abhinavagupta says the faculties of action must be distinguished from the faculties of perception.",
   "directed": "Now, Abhinavagupta says the faculties of action must be distinguished from the faculties of perception."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1106",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because acting and apprehending aren’t identical functions.",
   "directed": "Because acting and apprehending aren’t identical functions."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1107",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And he invokes an interesting distinction from the Vaiśeṣika system.",
   "directed": "And he invokes an interesting distinction from the Vaiśeṣika system."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1108",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Perceiving something, such as a visible form, is not classified there as an action in the same sense as moving.",
   "directed": "Perceiving something, such as a visible form, is not classified there as an action in the same sense as moving."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1109",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So we need an account of the specific instruments of activity.",
   "directed": "So we need an account of the specific instruments of activity."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1110",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Right.",
   "directed": "[short pause] Right."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1111",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But why five?",
   "directed": "But why five?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1112",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Why not seventeen?",
   "directed": "Why not seventeen?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1113",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Or three hundred?",
   "directed": "Or three hundred?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b1114",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Well, Abhinavagupta says there are five fundamental types of practical orientation.",
   "directed": "Well, Abhinavagupta says there are five fundamental types of practical orientation."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1115",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And the way he explains them is rather wonderful.",
   "directed": "And the way he explains them is rather wonderful."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1116",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "First: Giving something outward\nYou intend to expel something.",
   "directed": "First: Giving something outward\nYou intend to expel something."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1117",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Tyāga.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Tyāga."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1118",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 8",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Releasing.",
   "directed": "Releasing."
  },
  {
   "id": "b1119",
